PRODUCTION*Density / Ecological Urbanism (Taillandier Paris)Curator : @_mateo_btn_ Master 1 ENSA Versailles
@ensa_versailles The density of other surrounding villages was studied to set Dongziguan’s one. They wanted to have modular typologies to combine them in different ways and create new areas in the village, to create unique space into a modern pattern of living. They set the buildings to create space between them, with differents uses for each of them. Through the collaborative sessions with the inhabitants, they were able to propose differents uses for the types of outdoor spaces: relaxing, nature connection or storage for instance. The distance between the buildings allows public spaces. The urban fabric match perfectly with the surrounding land: mountains and water, a very traditional chinese landscape. Their work on the roofs really have an impact on the insertion of the village into its landscape.The interview is especially based on the analysis of the Dongziguan village affordable Housing 2016

Model by line+#China #contemporarychinesearchitecture #density #housing #architecture #lineplus #mengfanhao #architectureinterviews #lifestyle #collectivehousing #insideoutside #landscape #waterscape #publicspace #commons #collaborativearchitecture #context #history #materiality

